{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481945-b-s-compatible-blood-tenebrous-fan-rewrite","id":481945,"title":"B&S Compatible Blood Tenebrous Fan-rewrite","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-15T22:28:12-07:00","id":481945,"title":"B&S Compatible Blood Tenebrous Fan-rewrite","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CsAj4Mn8RcrobG38jaRBjjUqy2FpYG7v9KU6dGeunRg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> I would appreciate any thoughts. I kinda feel like the Essence Vitae mechanic is a little fiddly, but could be handled like other supernatural blood was handled in cWoD (yes, I realize there's a reason that system was dropped, but it was the closes analogue I could think of). I'm sure there's a brilliantly elegant solution just staring me in the face, but I would need other eyes to see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T23:21:17-07:00","id":481995,"title":"","content":"By default, Obfuscate works fine on spirits, so I'm not sure I see the benefit of the first part of the second level over, say, buying a single dot of Obfuscate. Similarly, they can feed on Spirits without a power (but risk becoming addicted to it, or having other weird effects), so maybe have the 4th dot power filter out those problems instead of being needed to allow it in the first place?<br /> <br /> I'm also not sure why you're putting detachment as a part of level 3 innately, though I do get why you used it for the 5th one. That is, I can see it causing detachment to become Claimed, but not sure why just going into the Shadow does.<br /> <br /> As for the essence vitae, I'd suggest just making it so sleeping at a Locus is what infuses the Vitae that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T00:51:44-07:00","id":482111,"title":"","content":"For me this feels like this should be a coil. Most of the powers are really Coil-Like. Other than that, why do you care for the Essence Vitae at all? What does it provide? In my opinion, additional bookkeeping with little benefit. Simply make it that all your vitae is Essence infused? Or make it 1 Vitae -&gt; Roll -&gt; Successes of Vitae may be used as essence right now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T10:03:26-07:00","id":482491,"title":"","content":"PenDragon actually made BT as a Coil, named the Coil of Divinity, which can be found in his google doc here; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1aeMOY7Ph7BCyz0IwBA70aaflEo-dMi2VG5tAT5_rkS0/edit#heading=h.jsk1qchpmgr\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...=h.jsk1qchpmgr</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T15:17:03-07:00","id":482845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481945-b-s-compatible-blood-tenebrous-fan-rewrite?p=481995#post481995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By default, Obfuscate works fine on spirits, so I'm not sure I see the benefit of the first part of the second level over, say, buying a single dot of Obfuscate. Similarly, they can feed on Spirits without a power (but risk becoming addicted to it, or having other weird effects), so maybe have the 4th dot power filter out those problems instead of being needed to allow it in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was unaware of either of those facts, actually. When I wrote this I was under the impression that the Unnatural Affinity merit didn't give you the ability to affect ephemeral beings, just the capability to gain sustenance from them, and that same merit only counted supernatural blood as Vitae for the purposes of feeding restrictions, but that it didn't feature the mechanics of addiction or any more strangeness than acquiring your unique blood-types. Can you point me to the discussion or page for these things (Obfuscate v. ephemeral beings and eating spirits)? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481945-b-s-compatible-blood-tenebrous-fan-rewrite?p=481995#post481995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not sure why you're putting detachment as a part of level 3 innately, though I do get why you used it for the 5th one. That is, I can see it causing detachment to become Claimed, but not sure why just going into the Shadow does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ST I wrote this for wondered if that wasn't a bit harsh as well, but I mentioned that the act of crossing the boundary is a decidedly supernatural act; as much as, if not more so than, experiencing intense physical trauma and surviving things that would hospitalize a human. In the sense that usage of the powers themselves remind you that you are not human, thus they invoke detachment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481945-b-s-compatible-blood-tenebrous-fan-rewrite?p=482111#post482111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me this feels like this should be a coil. Most of the powers are really Coil-Like. Other than that, why do you care for the Essence Vitae at all? What does it provide? In my opinion, additional bookkeeping with little benefit. Simply make it that all your vitae is Essence infused? Or make it 1 Vitae -&gt; Roll -&gt; Successes of Vitae may be used as essence right now?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a weakness for mechanics that substantiate fluff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Basically it exists so that as a vampire, you can have some form of immediate currency when dealing with the spirit world, but you have to be careful about it because this isn't what you do. Now that you're aware of this &quot;Other&quot; you have to manage how that interferes with both your character's Mask and your Dirge, because the thought was, the places that would have an appropriate Resonant condition are the places the character frequents. It gave you a way of being aware and watching what a vampire's feeding grounds were doing to the people around them. Which then facilitates the question: &quot;What do you do about it?&quot;<br /> <br /> That being said, I do like your idea of a roll, and I might have that be the 2-dot power. Riff on the idea of an intelligent hunter leaving a trail or trap. (Since Obfuscate works normally on spirits...)<br /> <br /> Also, at the time I wrote this I was thinking of straight conversation because the ST asked me to do it like, 2 sessions before it was necessary (and we still had a session where someone in the group had a power that no one knew what it did). So I did Discipline-to-Discipline conversion. That being said, I like PenDragon's Coil and may show it to my ST as an alternative for some of the NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:52:39-07:00","id":482950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ABenniton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/481945-b-s-compatible-blood-tenebrous-fan-rewrite?p=482845#post482845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was unaware of either of those facts, actually. When I wrote this I was under the impression that the Unnatural Affinity merit didn't give you the ability to affect ephemeral beings, just the capability to gain sustenance from them, and that same merit only counted supernatural blood as Vitae for the purposes of feeding restrictions, but that it didn't feature the mechanics of addiction or any more strangeness than acquiring your unique blood-types. Can you point me to the discussion or page for these things (Obfuscate v. ephemeral beings and eating spirits)? <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Both are listed in Book of Spirits, both in the section about Vampires. If you have trouble finding it, I can look later when I have access to my books.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The ST I wrote this for wondered if that wasn't a bit harsh as well, but I mentioned that the act of crossing the boundary is a decidedly supernatural act; as much as, if not more so than, experiencing intense physical trauma and surviving things that would hospitalize a human. In the sense that usage of the powers themselves remind you that you are not human, thus they invoke detachment. </div> </div> </div>I think that's more of an Integrity thing, though, not Humanity, in my opinion. Otherwise using most high dot disciplines would be a humanity break at that level, and that'd just be ridiculous. That is, I can't see turning into immaterial mist as more human than going into another realm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}